hy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 28757, "best_position": 2}, {"artist": "Romeo Santos", "streams": 20304, "best_position": 46}, {"artist": "BTS", "streams": 15124, "best_position": 7}, {"artist": "Aventura", "streams": 7576, "best_position": 42}, {"artist": "J Balvin", "streams": 6979, "best_position": 54}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Alvaro Diaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "r&b": {"genre": "r&b", "country_code": "do", "country_name": "Dominican Republic", "summary": "R&B is a musical genre that began to develop as a distinct style in the early 1950s. Originally known as rhythm and blues, it was primarily created by African American musicians and drew influence from both blues and early rock 'n' roll, with significant interaction between these genres. Over time, musicians from different backgrounds adopted the style and introduced new elements. In the 1950s, artists like Muddy Waters contributed to shaping the genre by emphasizing faster melodies and energetic rhythms.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Omar Courtz", "streams": 97315, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 28757, "best_position": 2}, {"artist": "Romeo Santos", "streams": 20304, "best_position": 46}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "st